      "prompt_sha1": "43aaf7f69ab5b26d5e9c77c1c10bf253f76649eb",
      "answer": "GPT-4 was fine-tuned using supervised fine-tuning (SFT) with demonstration data to imitate the behavior in the demonstrations [D3]. Additionally, a reward model (RM) was trained using ranking data to predict the average labeler’s preference for a given output, which was then used as a reward signal for reinforcement learning (specifically, the PPO algorithm) to further fine-tune the model [D3]. This process aimed to steer the model towards the desired behavior [D3]. The post-training alignment process also involved improving performance on measures of factuality and adherence to desired behavior [D4].",
