      "prompt_sha1": "c75e8c36806b66d5cf4f5996b254bd32d3895de9",
      "answer": "Rule-based reward models (RBRMs) are zero-shot GPT-4 classifiers used to provide an additional reward signal to the GPT-4 policy model during RLHF fine-tuning [D2]. They were used to steer the model towards appropriate refusals by rewarding GPT-4 for refusing harmful requests and not refusing safe ones [D3]. The RBRMs were part of a two-component safety approach that included safety-relevant RLHF training prompts [D2]. The RBRMs were enriched with data from production traffic and classified prompts into content categories [D5].",
