      "prompt_sha1": "fcd925d24121182c2d093353dddefe42e03ffd9a",
      "answer": "The authors checked for contamination by running variants of exams and benchmarks with the contaminated questions removed and reporting the lower score of the two [D1]. They also conducted contamination checks for test data appearing in the training set for each benchmark [D3]. For specific benchmarks like GSM-8K, they included part of the training set in GPT-4’s pre-training mix and used chain-of-thought prompting [D5]. The results were considered representative of the model's performance without contamination [D1].",
